On Jul 3, 2009, at 8:37 PM, Gabor Grothendieck wrote:

> Consider the following code using the H2 database where we are using  
> the built in BOD data frame.  Note that the column names come out in  
> upper case.

SQL is by definition case-agnostic, so that is to be expected... (Some  
DBMS break that rule at their own risk ...).


>  I have inserted a print statement into dbWriteTable and you can see  
> the sql statement that dbWriteTable generates.  Shouldn't that sql  
> statement have double quotes around the column names?

The logic in RJDBC is that if an identifier is of the form  
<letter><letter/number/_> then it won't be quoted. At least in  
standard SQL it should make no difference. (However, your post made me  
think about this -- and in the cases of keywords the current logic may  
not be sufficient ...).

Cheers,
Simon



