Just in case the motivation isn't clear consider this sqldf
statement using the CRAN version of sqldf package which
uses RSQLite/sqlite.  BOD is a built in data frame that comes
with R.  Note that the column names are
produced in a case sensitive manner (Time__1 is due to the
fact that Time is an SQL keyword).

But after that we run the development
version using RJDBC/H2 and note how the column
names become capitalized after we switched databases.

> library(sqldf)
> sqldf("select * from BOD")
  Time__1 demand
1       1    8.3
2       2   10.3
3       3   19.0
4       4   16.0
5       5   15.6
6       7   19.8

> # following is from development code (not on CRAN)
> library(H2)
> library(sqldf)
> sqldf("select * from BOD") # uses RJDBC/H2
  TIME DEMAND
1    1    8.3
2    2   10.3
3    3   19.0
4    4   16.0
5    5   15.6
6    7   19.8


