Simon,

Yes, you are right:  Shift-Alt works as expected when I use either 
fluxbox or the KDE window manager.  It seems the Shift-Win-Alt 
combination is only necessary with the Gnome window manager in its 
default configuration, which is what I have been using recently.  Gnome 
comes with a keyboard utility that I had played with a week or so ago in 
order to try to get Shift-Alt to modify selections.  Presumably it's 
possible to fix using that utility, but none of the built-in choices I 
tried seemed to work.  I had also noticed when searching online for a 
solution that there seemed to be a lot of complaints about Gnome's 
default keyboard setup.

I had thought that the call to xmodmap during startup had made the 
changes, but that seems not to be the case because the xmodmap settings 
are the same when I am using fluxbox.  So, I think you are right; Gnome 
seems to be hogging the Shift-Alt combination for itself, at least under 
the default configuration.

Thanks for your help.

Bill


