Hello,

In the latest Rserve client, i created an RList using the  RList(size,
true) constructor.
I then proceeded to add elements, i.e
for(i in 1:n) rlistobj.add(Obj)

and then seperatley added names

for(i in 1:n) rlistObj.setKeyAt(i,name(i))


However, the first n are valid, the the names vector is double the
size of the list.The extra being null.
This is because in RList.java
	public void setKeyAt(int i, String value) {
		if (i < 0) return;
		if (names==null)
			names = new Vector();
		if (names.size() < size()) names.setSize(size());
		if (i < size()) names.add(i, value);
	}

names.add(i,value) /inserts/ at position i, but does not replace it.

I changed the 'add' to 'set' and all works now.

Hope this helps
Regards
Saptarshi

