> 2
> I think the internal coding for NA is supposed to be -128 (judging  
> from
> the src) not 2
> */
>

It's a bit hairy - R uses 0/1/2 but I was trying to be smart in  
REXPLogical and interpret non-zero values as TRUE except for the  
special NA value. We could mimic  R more closely by using 2 for  
REXPLogical.NA - it may be a bit safer, but the more general  
interpretation of values by REXPLogical makes is more dangerous. One  
option is still to set REXPLogical.NA = 2 so always use the constants  
instead of the raw values asa this may change.

Cheers,
Simon


