Hi again,

I've put a patch here 
(http://addictedtor.free.fr/misc/rosuda/wrapping.diff) that implements a 
wrap method for REngine which takes an Object and gives back a REXP.

If it is already a REXP, it is returned verbatim, otherwise if it is a 
primitive type (int,long,short,double,String,float) or an array of 
those, it is converted to the appropriate REXP subclass.

In addition, for the JRIEngine an attempt is made to convert the object 
to a "jObjRef" object in R

BeanShell> r.wrap( 10 )
org.rosuda.REngine.REXPInteger@510e39[1]
BeanShell> r.wrap( 10.0 )
org.rosuda.REngine.REXPDouble@61373f[1]
BeanShell> r.wrap( "foobar" )
org.rosuda.REngine.REXPString@1f44ec7[1]


BeanShell> p = new Point( 10, 10 )
java.awt.Point[x=10,y=10]
BeanShell> ref = r.wrap( p )
org.rosuda.REngine.REXPReference@1362a63{eng=org.rosuda.REngine.JRI.JRIEngine@867fc9,h=171890632}
BeanShell> r.assign( "p", ref, r.globalEnv )

 > p$move( 40L, 30L )
 > p
[1] "Java-Object{java.awt.Point[x=40,y=30]}"

BeanShell> p
java.awt.Point[x=40,y=30]


